{# The controls that narrow a list, and nothing else. It fills `canvas.filters`
   (D8/D15): the two-column relation between the controls and the results is the
   canvas's, so this component owns no layout, no results region and no summary.
   The human asked for Linear's model — narrowing is done in an aside and what
   has been chosen is stated separately, above the rows — rather than for one row
   of pills doing both jobs at once (C22).

   NOTHING HERE SAYS "FACET". The aside is where a list is narrowed; whether that
   narrowing is a facet, an exposed filter or a saved view is a wiring question
   this ticket deliberately leaves open, and the vocabulary should not pre-empt
   it (D8).

   THE PANEL COLLAPSES BY COMPOSING `bb_theme:collapsible` rather than by
   carrying a second collapse of its own. That component is a native
   <details>/<summary> for a measured reason this panel shares exactly: Storybook
   never calls Drupal.attachBehaviors, so a scripted collapse would be a dead
   control on the surface the human reviews on — a click that answers with
   nothing is worse than no affordance at all. Composing it means there is ONE
   collapse mechanism in this theme, and the `Filters` heading IS the <summary>.
   The heading uses the existing body typography inside the summary.

   `collapsed` rather than `open`, because the panel's resting state is EXPANDED:
   a filter panel nobody can see is not a filter panel. The prop names the
   deviation from that resting state, the way `sidebar`'s does. It is passed
   through as `open: not collapsed`, so an absent prop leaves the panel open.
   What it no longer does is give the region its width back: the 192px track
   belongs to `canvas` now, which is the price of the aside not owning a layout.

   The heading is what the collapse is operated by, so a caller that omits
   `title` gets a chevron-only toggle.

   Spacing is the token scale (D16). Nothing here fetches, posts or persists a
   view.

   `layout: bar` IS THE SEARCH TOOLBAR above the rows (BB-592): not an aside,
   no heading and no collapse, the same surface as the panel, and its controls in
   ONE row — the first (the search) grows and wraps onto its own line before it
   would overflow, the later ones (the sort) keep their own width capped at the
   row. Its fields live OUTSIDE the exposed <form> (bound by the HTML `form`
   attribute), so BEF's autosubmit, which watches only the form's own elements,
   never sees them; the bar submits their form itself: a select on `change`, a
   text field 500ms after the last keystroke, and never the same value twice, so
   an Enter (which already submits natively) is not followed by a second request.
   `panel` is the default and the aside it always was, now filled with `bg-app`
   so it reads as a surface on the `bg-surface` main area. #}
{% set filters_controls %}{% block controls %}{{ controls }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{% set filters_actions %}{% block actions %}{{ actions }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{#- The bar and the toolbar submit their own fields: a select on change, a
    text field 500ms after the last keystroke, never the same value twice. -#}
{% set send_attributes %}x-data="{ send(field) { if (field.form && field.dataset.sent !== field.value) { field.dataset.sent = field.value; field.form.requestSubmit(); } } }" @change="['search', 'text'].includes($event.target.type) || send($event.target)" @input.debounce.500ms="['search', 'text'].includes($event.target.type) && send($event.target)" @keydown.enter="['search', 'text'].includes($event.target.type) && ($event.target.dataset.sent = $event.target.value)"{% endset %}
{% if layout|default('panel') == 'bar' %}
<div{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass([
    'flex', 'flex-row', 'flex-wrap', 'items-end', 'gap-stack', 'p-stack', 'bg-app', 'border', 'border-border-2', 'rounded-sm',
    '*:first:flex-1', '*:first:basis-40', '*:first:min-w-0', '*:not-first:shrink-0', '*:not-first:max-w-full',
  ]) }} role="search"
  {%- if label %} aria-label="{{ label }}"{% endif %}
  {{ send_attributes }}>
  {{- filters_controls -}}
</div>
{% elseif layout == 'toolbar' %}
{#- The board filter bar: no surface, one centred row of at least 36 px that
    wraps only when narrow. The controls group leads with the search (240 px);
    `actions` is a second group the row pushes to the right end
    (justify-between, no outer margin). -#}
<div{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass([
    'flex', 'flex-row', 'flex-wrap', 'items-center', 'justify-between', 'gap-inline', 'min-h-9', 'min-w-0',
  ]) }} role="search"
  {%- if label %} aria-label="{{ label }}"{% endif %}
  {{ send_attributes }}>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-inline min-w-0 *:first:w-60 *:first:shrink-0">{{ filters_controls }}</div>
  {%- if filters_actions|striptags|trim is not empty %}
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-inline">{{ filters_actions }}</div>
  {%- endif %}
</div>
{% else %}
<aside{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass([
    'p-stack', 'bg-app', 'border', 'border-border-2', 'rounded-sm',
  ]) }}
  {%- if label %} aria-label="{{ label }}"{% endif %}>
  {% embed 'bb_theme:collapsible' with {
    open: not collapsed,
    attributes: create_attribute(),
  } %}
    {% block label %}<span class="text-body-strong text-title">{{ title }}</span>{% endblock %}
    {% block content %}
      <div class="flex flex-col items-stretch gap-group">{{ filters_controls }}</div>
    {% endblock %}
  {% endembed %}
</aside>
{% endif %}
